                ;; The build-time reader for committed `spec/` data
                ;; (day8/re-frame2-spec-resource). Both macros named under
                ;; the `../spec` root below go through it, and it is on
                ;; this classpath so they can: it owns the shadow-cljs
                ;; recording read, the non-ClojureScript walk-up fallback,
                ;; and — the reason it is ONE namespace rather than a
                ;; helper copied into each consumer — the cold-load
                ;; resolution of `shadow.resource/slurp-resource`, which
                ;; two independent resolvers race however carefully each
                ;; one guards itself. JVM-only source; nothing compilable
                ;; into a bundle.
                "spec-resource/src"
                ;; `spec/` as a classpath ROOT — the one root under which
                ;; every committed spec-side DATA file a build inlines is
                ;; resolvable. Data only: no sources, nothing compilable,
                ;; and no production build requires any of it.
                ;;
                ;; Two consumers today, both macros that inline a
                ;; committed file at macro-expansion time — which by
                ;; itself hides that file from the build, because a
                ;; ClojureScript compile that caches the namespace has no
                ;; edge back to the bytes it froze. A DATA-ONLY edit then
                ;; leaves the cached namespace asserting the PREVIOUS
                ;; values: a confident green over an expectation nobody is
                ;; checking. Reading through `shadow.resource/slurp-resource`
                ;; instead records the file's classpath path and
                ;; last-modified against the compiling namespace, so the
                ;; data participates in that namespace's cache key. Both
                ;; consumers reach that reader through the one namespace
                ;; above, never directly.
                ;;
                ;;   conformance/freehand/fixtures/*.edn — inlined by
                ;;     `re-frame.freehand.conformance/fixture`.
                ;;   api-manifest-metadata.edn — inlined by
                ;;     `re-frame.api-manifest.cljs-publics`.
                ;;
                ;; ONE root rather than one per consumer: nesting
                ;; `spec/conformance` inside `spec` would index the same
                ;; files under two resource names, and each consumer
                ;; already names its own path below the root.
                ;;
